From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: the screen saver shows NickelOS's wallpapers, or the
 user's own pictures

The screen saver was a slideshow of the account's Pictures folder (0105),
with the default wallpaper when it had fewer than two pictures (0114).
It shows NickelOS's wallpapers now, the nine of Wallpaper & style's
NickelOS collection (collection.json, 0116), in random order and in dark
mode with the wave's dark twin (Dresden, 2026-11-05). A switch in the
screen saver's settings, "Your own pictures" (nickel.screen_saver.own_pictures,
off), shows the Pictures folder instead, with NickelOS's wallpapers while
it has fewer than two pictures. Turning it on or off makes the list again
at once, for the next screen saver. The preview card says which (NickelOS
wallpapers, or Pictures folder) and shows the default wallpaper's
thumbnail in place of ChromeOS's coast photo.

The slideshow fills the screen as ChromeOS's own does, where the managed
slideshow it is made from fitted every picture with bars: on an ultrawide
screen the pictures had wide black bars beside them. A picture of the
screen's orientation fills it, cropped at the edges; a portrait photo on a
landscape screen still fits whole.

